Use `@Cacheable` on a service method:

```java
@Service
public class ProductService {
    @Cacheable(cacheNames = "products", key = "#id")
    public Product getProduct(Long id) {
        // expensive DB call
    }
}
```

On the first call for a given `id`, the result is stored in the cache under that key; subsequent calls with the same `id` return the cached value without invoking the method.
